1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:02,120
There is a giant black hole at

2
00:00:02,120 --> 00:00:04,140
the center of our galaxy. So why

3
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:05,765
hasn't it swallowed us?

4
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:09,000
It packs roughly four million times the

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,020
mass of our Sun. But mass alone

6
00:00:11,020 --> 00:00:13,190
does not tell the whole story.

7
00:00:13,953 --> 00:00:16,373
Black holes do not magically suck everything

8
00:00:16,373 --> 00:00:19,193
in. From far away, their gravity depends

9
00:00:19,193 --> 00:00:21,248
on mass and distance.

10
00:00:22,003 --> 00:00:24,323
Imagine replacing the Sun with a black

11
00:00:24,323 --> 00:00:26,763
hole of exactly the same mass. Earth

12
00:00:26,763 --> 00:00:28,398
would keep its orbit.

13
00:00:29,153 --> 00:00:31,213
We would lose sunlight, which would be

14
00:00:31,213 --> 00:00:33,433
disastrous for life. But we would not

15
00:00:33,433 --> 00:00:35,648
suddenly spiral into the center.

16
00:00:36,403 --> 00:00:38,928
Our galaxy's central black hole is about

17
00:00:38,928 --> 00:00:41,183
twenty six thousand light years away. It

18
00:00:41,183 --> 00:00:43,223
is not about to swallow Earth.

19
00:00:43,987 --> 00:00:46,727
To understand an orbit, ask about mass,

20
00:00:46,727 --> 00:00:49,287
distance, and motion. The words black hole

21
00:00:49,287 --> 00:00:50,632
are not enough.

22
00:00:51,387 --> 00:00:54,387
The real mystery begins much closer. What

23
00:00:54,387 --> 00:00:55,767
would happen if you crossed the point

24
00:00:55,767 --> 00:00:57,182
of no return?
